\ Give each of m months a distinct canonical name from indices 1..47.
\ Names are selected in lexicographic order without replacement.
\ There are 47!/(47-m)! distinct sequences, where 3 <= m <= 47.
\ This may exceed M, so use the canonical wide equal-choice mechanism.
\ The shared year-structure sauce uses bowl 5 with seal 33.
\ The ordinal position of a month is not its canonical name index.
\ Month weaving will later determine the ordinal of each calendar day.
\ CAL compilation has not yet been verified.

A month name assignment is a thing with
  a number called name index.

The chosen month names are some month name assignments.
The new month name assignment is a month name assignment.
The examined month name assignment is a month name assignment.

A month name choice has
  a number called names chosen,
  a number called candidate index,
  a number called used status,
  a number called selection success,
  a number called available names,
  a number called names still required,
  a wide quantity called total sequences,
  a wide quantity called tail sequences,
  a wide quantity called remaining rank.

The month name choice is a month name choice.
The requested month ordinal is a number.
The requested month name index is a number.

To count all month name sequences:
  Put "1" into the month name choice's total sequences.
  Put 47 into the month name choice's available names.
  Put the selected month count into the month name choice's names still required.
  Loop.
    If the month name choice's names still required is 0, break.
    Multiply the month name choice's total sequences by the month name choice's available names.
    Subtract 1 from the month name choice's available names.
    Subtract 1 from the month name choice's names still required.
  Repeat.

\ Once the next name has been fixed, P(46-chosen,m-chosen-1)
\ name sequences remain in the lexicographic block.
To count month name suffixes:
  Put "1" into the month name choice's tail sequences.
  Put 47 into the month name choice's available names.
  Subtract the month name choice's names chosen from the month name choice's available names.
  Subtract 1 from the month name choice's available names.
  Put the selected month count into the month name choice's names still required.
  Subtract the month name choice's names chosen from the month name choice's names still required.
  Subtract 1 from the month name choice's names still required.
  Loop.
    If the month name choice's names still required is 0, break.
    Multiply the month name choice's tail sequences by the month name choice's available names.
    Subtract 1 from the month name choice's available names.
    Subtract 1 from the month name choice's names still required.
  Repeat.

To inspect the candidate month name:
  Put 0 into the month name choice's used status.
  Put the chosen month names' first into the examined month name assignment.
  Loop.
    If the examined month name assignment is nil, break.
    If the examined month name assignment's name index is the month name choice's candidate index,
      put 1 into the month name choice's used status; break.
    Put the examined month name assignment's next into the examined month name assignment.
  Repeat.

To remember the new month name:
  Allocate memory for the new month name assignment.
  Put the month name choice's candidate index into the new month name assignment's name index.
  Append the new month name assignment to the chosen month names.
  Add 1 to the month name choice's names chosen.

To select the next month name:
  Count month name suffixes.
  Put 1 into the month name choice's candidate index.
  Loop.
    If the month name choice's candidate index is greater than 47, break.
    Inspect the candidate month name.
    If the month name choice's used status is 1,
      add 1 to the month name choice's candidate index; repeat.
    If the month name choice's tail sequences is numerically smaller than the month name choice's remaining rank,
      subtract the month name choice's tail sequences from the month name choice's remaining rank;
      add 1 to the month name choice's candidate index;
      repeat.
    Remember the new month name.
    Break.
  Repeat.

To select month names from a wide quantity:
  Put 0 into the month name choice's selection success.
  Destroy the chosen month names.
  If the selected month count is less than 1, exit.
  If the selected month count is greater than 47, exit.
  If the wide quantity is "0", exit.
  Count all month name sequences.
  If the month name choice's total sequences is numerically smaller than the wide quantity, exit.
  Put the wide quantity into the month name choice's remaining rank.
  Put 0 into the month name choice's names chosen.
  Loop.
    If the month name choice's names chosen is the selected month count, break.
    Select the next month name.
    If the month name choice's candidate index is greater than 47, exit.
  Repeat.
  Put 1 into the month name choice's selection success.

\ Rebuild the shared structure sauce whenever a gate walk has run.
To choose the canonical month names:
  Prepare the year structure sauce.
  Count all month name sequences.
  Put 5 into the seal inquiry's bowl identity.
  Put 33 into the seal inquiry's seal number.
  Begin a seal inquiry.
  Choose an equal option given the month name choice's total sequences.
  Select month names from the seal inquiry's selected quantity.

To read the requested month name:
  Put 0 into the requested month name index.
  Put 1 into a month name ordinal number.
  Put the chosen month names' first into the examined month name assignment.
  Loop.
    If the examined month name assignment is nil, break.
    If the month name ordinal number is the requested month ordinal,
      put the examined month name assignment's name index into the requested month name index; break.
    Put the examined month name assignment's next into the examined month name assignment.
    Add 1 to the month name ordinal number.
  Repeat.
